// The played bed with a flowering understory at the edges of the nest band
// -- round 29's bed question, 2026-09-11.
//
// **Why this file exists.** B1 gave the flitter a float
// (`Reports/evolution-lab-flight-design-2026-09-11.md`), and the float works:
// it fires, it steers, it lands on the bloom, and a guard shows it closing on
// a flower no walk or hop can reach. What it did **not** buy was meals. The
// measurement that says why is not about the animal at all:
//
//   seed   standing flowers on the bare bed   flitter flower_visits   born
//     1                 23                            76               3
//     2                  6                             8               0
//     3                  6                             5               0
//
// **The payoff tracks the flower supply, not the animal.** That is the
// design's own §6 condition -- *"it becomes the right lever after B1"* -- and
// the owner's own third option, "or we need a better bed for the flitter".
//
// **What changes, and it is four lines.** `played_bed.ron` exactly, plus four
// scramblers -- the only shipped plant that carries a real flower count
// (round 27: a median 60 standing flowers against `played_bed`'s 16) -- at
// **140, 170, 340 and 372**.
//
// **The columns are the whole design of this file, and they are constrained
// from both ends.** The colony lands at x=256 at frame 6,000 and
// `found_colony_of` needs bare footing, so `played_bed.ron`'s header keeps
// columns **180-330** clear; `played_bed_scrambler.ron` put scramblers at 195
// and 315 and seated **2 founders of 52**. So the flowers cannot go in the
// band. But the flitters are founded *in* the band, their eye reaches 32
// cells, and `played_bed`'s nearest plants to the nest are the shrub at 180
// and the grass at 330 -- **76 columns from where the animals start**, which
// is more than twice the eye. Four flowering clumps at 140/170/340/372 are
// the closest a flower can legally stand to the nest: outside the band by 10
// and 10, and 86 columns of flowering ground closer than the old nearest
// bloom.
//
// **The founder count is the gate on this file, not a footnote.**
// `played_bed` seats 33 / 13 / 18 on seeds 1 / 2 / 3 and that spread is a
// real property of it; a variant that seats materially fewer has bought
// flowers with the colony and is not the bed the owner plants. Read
// `labforage`'s founder line at frame 6,100 before reading anything else
// here.
//
// Everything else is `played_bed.ron` unchanged, including the tree, so a
// difference between the two files is the understory and nothing else.
(
    name: "played_bed_understory",
    title: "THE PLAYED BED WITH A FLOWERING UNDERSTORY",
    question: "The owner's mix with four flowering clumps just outside the nest band -- can a flitter make a living on it, and does the colony still seat?",
    bed: (
        width: 512,
        height: 320,
        soil_depth: 80,
        ground_y: 160,
        compartments: 1,
        founders: 0,
        species: "grass",
        colonies: 0,
        colony_ants: 52,
        colony_species: "ant",
        predators: 0,
        lamp_spacing: 33,
        seed: 1,
        extra_walls: [],
    ),
    settings: [],
    placements: [
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 25),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 50),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 75),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 105),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 130),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 155),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 180),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 330),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 355),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 380),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 410),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 435),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 465),
        Plant(species: "scrambler", x: 15),
        Plant(species: "scrambler", x: 118),
        Plant(species: "scrambler", x: 395),
        Plant(species: "scrambler", x: 490),
        Plant(species: "tree",      x: 455),
        // The four this file is for. Outside 180-330 by ten columns at each
        // end -- see the header for why that margin is the whole design.
        Plant(species: "scrambler", x: 140),
        Plant(species: "scrambler", x: 170),
        Plant(species: "scrambler", x: 340),
        Plant(species: "scrambler", x: 372),
    ],
    timeline: [
        // Identical to `played_bed.ron`'s own entry -- see that file's header
        // for why the band must stay bare rather than being swept with an
        // explicit `Clear`.
        (at: 6000, every: 0, until: 0, what: Colony(species: "ant", x: 256, count: 52)),
    ],
    horizon: 120000,
)
